# Echoes of Termina — repository-wide ignore rules
# =============================================================================
# This is the only shared .gitignore. Each PlatformIO project under Firmware/
# also keeps a two-line local file for its own .pio/.vscode noise, but anything
# that could appear anywhere in the tree belongs HERE instead of being copied
# into the nested files.
#
# Layout:
#   1. Python                 caches and packaging by-products
#   2. Build / release output generated artifacts, never source
#   3. Firmware               PlatformIO build data and capture logs
#   4. KiCad                  per-machine files, backups and locks
#   5. Editors / OS           local tool state
#   6. Demo projects          shipped empty until DRM-free content lands
#   7. Deliberately tracked   things that LOOK generated but must stay in Git
# =============================================================================

# ── 1. Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Byte-code caches and editable-install metadata are regenerated on the next
# import; they cause merge noise and never belong in history.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Virtual environments: exact interpreter + package set is a property of each
# machine, not of the project.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ── 2. Build / release output ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PyInstaller spec files and build trees, plus the zipped editor release.
# build_release.py writes its ZIP into Executable/echoes/dist/, which the bare
# dist/ pattern already covers (dist/build/ match at any depth).
dist/
build/
*.spec

# ── 3. Firmware (PlatformIO) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .pio/ holds the downloaded toolchain and every per-env build object.
# compile_commands.json is machine-specific build metadata.
# *.log comes from tools/serial_capture.py (e.g. serial_click2.log, serial_flash.log).
.pio/
compile_commands.json
*.log

# ── 4. KiCad ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backup folders, project locks, the footprint cache and per-save backups are
# all local working state.
*-backups/
*.lck
fp-info-cache
*.kicad_pcb-bak
*.kicad_sch-bak
*.kicad_sym-bak
*.kicad_pro-bak
# NOTE: *.kicad_prl is intentionally TRACKED (board layout/layer state ships
# with the project). Ignoring it here would do nothing for already-tracked
# files and would be wrong: it needs `git rm --cached` first if that decision
# is ever reversed.

# ── 5. Editors / OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/.browse.c_cpp.db*
.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/ipch
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── 6. Demo projects ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The release ships projects/ EMPTY for now: Keep the README so the folder
# survives a fresh clone; ignore everything else under it until the DRM-free
# content set is added. Local test projects (e.g. "Lost Woods") stay on disk
# but never reach Git.
Executable/echoes/projects/*
!Executable/echoes/projects/README.txt

# ── 7. Deliberately tracked — do not "fix" these with ignore rules ───────────
# These names look generated but are required to build, document or reproduce:
#   Firmware/echoes_of_termina/boards/*.json        board defs for each env
#   Firmware/echoes_of_termina/partitions_*.csv     partition tables per flash size
#   Firmware/echoes_of_termina/docs/**              flowcharts + two-button UI doc
#   Firmware/echoes_of_termina/tools/*.py           serial_capture, make_flowcharts
#   Hardware/**/production/**                       fab outputs (BOM, netlist, ZIP)
#   Datasheets/**                                   component reference PDFs
#   Executable/echoes/projects/README.txt           placeholder that keeps the folder
#   Firmware/**/.vscode/extensions.json             shared extension recommendations
